<p>If the hard disk is installed on the printer, you can create and register 
 image overlays.</p>
<h2>What Is Image Overlay?</h2>
<p>This function allows you to create form data that is usable with page 
 frames, so you can make settings for combining and printing documents.</p>
<p>For details about using image overlay, see the operating instructions 
 provided with the printer. </p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Printing is not possible using this driver; only 
 image overlay registration can be performed. For details about print-capable 
 emulations, see the operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
<li><p>Use Web Image Monitor to confirm or delete registered 
 image overlay settings.<br/>
 For details, see the Web Image Monitor help.</p></li>
<li><p>Always return to normal printing after registering 
 an image overlay.</p></li>
<li><p>Always return to a resolution of 600 dpi, regardless 
 of the driver setting.</p></li>
<li><p>The toner save function may become invalid.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating frame data for use in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Setup</span> menu 
 of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Store as Image Overlay</span> 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type: </span>list.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> 
 button to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Register Image Overlay</span> 
 dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Enter a number for the image overlay in <span class="Term-Soft">Registration Number:</span>.<br/>
 Enter a number between 1 and 300.<br/>
 Registration is cancelled if you enter a number that is already registered. 
 To register a new image overlay with an existing number, use Web Image 
 Monitor to delete the first registration.</p></li>
<li><p>Enter a name for the image overlay in <span class="Term-Soft">Registration 
 Name:</span>.<br/>
 You can enter up to 64 single-byte or 32 double-byte characters except 
 double quotation marks.</p></li>
<li><p>Select an orientation in the <span class="Term-Soft">Image 
 Overlay Orientation:</span> area.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
<li><p>The image overlay data is saved on the printer's 
 hard disk.</p></li>
</ol>
